cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PixPoint in a publication, please cite it as below: until PixPoint has a software paper of its own, that is the SBi3PCF paper it was developed for. Please also name the PixPoint version you used, cite its Zenodo archive (10.5281/zenodo.23915406) and cite the papers behind the estimators you used (see the Citing page of the documentation)."
type: software
title: "PixPoint: correlation functions of HEALPix maps on GPUs and CPUs"
abstract: "PixPoint measures two-point, three-point, integrated three-point and one-point statistics of cosmological fields on HEALPix maps (cosmic shear, galaxy clustering, galaxy-galaxy lensing, convergence). The pixel pairs of a footprint are found once and reused for every map; measurements run on CPUs via Numba and on NVIDIA GPUs via CuPy."
